            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 679)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Web reviews ask for the passphrase by default.</b> &#8220;Require the passphrase&#8221; is now on unless you turn it off, and the setting is remembered. It is the same four words shown in the Shared Review panel &#8212; send the link, give the words another way. Passphrase links are short links now, too.</li>
<li><b>End Review ends it for everyone, straight away.</b> Pages that have the review open close within a few seconds instead of playing on from what they had loaded, and the copy saved in each viewer&#8217;s browser is deleted. Tick &#8220;Viewers keep their saved copy after it ends&#8221; if you want it to stay watchable, read-only.</li>
<li><b>On the web:</b> guests must enter a name to join (no Cancel, no &#8220;Guest&#8221;), the passphrase typed where the name goes is refused, and an ended review says plainly that notes and marks are closed.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
